Install STACK SymPy and AI Feedback in your Quarto project, and install SymPy in the Python environment Quarto uses:
quarto add Erasmus-CTM/stack-sympy
quarto add Erasmus-CTM/ai-feedback
python -m pip install 'sympy==1.13.3'
Add the question filter to _quarto.yml:
filters:
  - stack-sympy
Use a Moodle STACK export whose root is &lt;quiz&gt; and whose questions use &lt;question type="stack"&gt;. Keep the normal question, input, PRT, deployed-seed, and qtest elements. Point a stack-question block at its XML path and exact &lt;name&gt;&lt;text&gt;…&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/name&gt;. The filter embeds a selected question and precomputes the requested variants when Quarto renders. The original XML remains the source of truth and can be imported back into Moodle.
