    &lt;deployedseed&gt;29&lt;/deployedseed&gt;
    &lt;deployedseed&gt;47&lt;/deployedseed&gt;
    &lt;qtest&gt;
      &lt;testcase&gt;1&lt;/testcase&gt;
      &lt;description&gt;Expanded polynomial&lt;/description&gt;
      &lt;testinput&gt;
        &lt;name&gt;ans&lt;/name&gt;
        &lt;value&gt;ta&lt;/value&gt;
      &lt;/testinput&gt;
      &lt;expected&gt;
        &lt;name&gt;prt1&lt;/name&gt;
        &lt;expectedscore&gt;1.0000000&lt;/expectedscore&gt;
        &lt;expectedpenalty&gt;0.0000000&lt;/expectedpenalty&gt;
        &lt;expectedanswernote&gt;prt1-0-T&lt;/expectedanswernote&gt;
      &lt;/expected&gt;
    &lt;/qtest&gt;
    &lt;qtest&gt;
      &lt;testcase&gt;2&lt;/testcase&gt;
      &lt;description&gt;Equivalent but still factored&lt;/description&gt;
      &lt;testinput&gt;
        &lt;name&gt;ans&lt;/name&gt;
        &lt;value&gt;(x+a)*(x+b)&lt;/value&gt;
      &lt;/testinput&gt;
      &lt;expected&gt;
        &lt;name&gt;prt1&lt;/name&gt;
        &lt;expectedscore&gt;0.5000000&lt;/expectedscore&gt;
        &lt;expectedpenalty&gt;0.1000000&lt;/expectedpenalty&gt;
        &lt;expectedanswernote&gt;prt1-0-F | prt1-1-T&lt;/expectedanswernote&gt;
      &lt;/expected&gt;
    &lt;/qtest&gt;
    &lt;qtest&gt;
      &lt;testcase&gt;3&lt;/testcase&gt;
      &lt;description&gt;Incorrect middle coefficient&lt;/description&gt;
      &lt;testinput&gt;
        &lt;name&gt;ans&lt;/name&gt;
        &lt;value&gt;x^2+(a+b+1)*x+a*b&lt;/value&gt;
      &lt;/testinput&gt;
      &lt;expected&gt;
        &lt;name&gt;prt1&lt;/name&gt;
        &lt;expectedscore&gt;0.0000000&lt;/expectedscore&gt;
        &lt;expectedpenalty&gt;0.1000000&lt;/expectedpenalty&gt;
        &lt;expectedanswernote&gt;prt1-0-F | prt1-1-F&lt;/expectedanswernote&gt;
      &lt;/expected&gt;
    &lt;/qtest&gt;
  &lt;/question&gt;
&lt;/quiz&gt;

Run quarto render, then serve the generated site over HTTP. The README also covers local development setup.
The learner submits in two steps: Validate answers parses the current fields and displays the expression form (for example, x+x rather than a simplified 2*x), then Check answer grades that validated response. Editing any field invalidates the preview, so the learner must validate again. This explicit check mirrors the question input verification setting and helps learners catch syntax errors before grading. The polynomial example sets &lt;insertstars&gt;1&lt;/insertstars&gt;, so x**2+8x+15 previews as one sum and receives full credit in its first variant.
Below a rendered question, Show source reveals its authored Quarto fenced block and Show STACK source reveals the original XML file contents. Both panels start closed; they are available for inspecting and copying a working example.
The options are file and question (required), seed (signed integer, default 1), variants (1–20, default 1), review (true or false, default false), and diagnostics (true or false, default false). feedback: true opts a card into the shared AI Feedback extension; cards without it need no AI dependency. Install both extensions in the same project; feedback requires AI Feedback 0.8.0+ and Quarto 1.8.27+. context: auto (default) uses nearby visible prose; context: none omits it; context: id1,id2 includes tagged blocks such as ::: {#id1 .ai-context} (.ai-feedback-context and .math-exercise-context are shared aliases). feedback-language sets the explanation language (default document lang). feedback-policy selects an existing named policy from ai-feedback.policy-files or page policy files. A stable label targets exercise-specific policy settings; otherwise the card ID is used. The shared mathematics policy (math-exercise) supplies the default hints and is also the YAML integration namespace for STACK cards. A fixed seed reproduces a variant within this implementation. It does not promise the same pseudo-random sequence as Moodle’s Maxima backend.
Feedback uses a learner’s current answer, visible question text and selected context. A preceding matching Check answer can contribute minimal result status, finite score; XML, source panels, teacher answers, qtests, grader configuration, grader feedback messages and answer notes are excluded. It never grades a response or replaces Validate answers and Check answer. The shared settings panel lets a learner choose copy-prompt mode or configure their own compatible provider; no API key is placed in the page. The same explicit teaching policies are inherited across integrations, using math-exercise for STACK’s mathematics policy namespace.

